    "title": "When is the 2026 Boston Marathon? Times, route map, how to watch",
    "text": "April 13, 2026, 11:50 a.m. ETMarathon Monday is on the horizon.In just seven days, hundreds of thousands of people will flock to Massachusetts to cheer on, volunteer at and run in the 130th Boston Marathon.The annual race, which boasts itself as the oldest marathon in the world, is one of seven World Marathon Majors.Every year, the Boston Marathon falls on Patriots' Day, a Massachusetts holiday commemorating the battles of Lexington and Concord.The 26.2-mile course begins in Hopkinton, a town west of Boston, and takes runners through several areas before concluding in the city's Back Bay neighborhood.Here's what to know about this year's Boston Marathon, including how to watch from home.When is the 2026 Boston Marathon?This year, the Boston Marathon falls on Monday, April 20.The historic race is held annually on Patriots' Day, which is the third Monday in April, so it is often referred to as Marathon Monday.What time does the Boston Marathon start?The Boston Marathon begins in waves to stagger runners on the course.The first runners are in the following divisions: wheelchair men and women, handcycles and duos, professional men and women and para athletics. After that, there are six starting waves for the remaining participants.See the full start times by category:Wheelchair Men - 9:06 a.m.Wheelchair Women - 9:09 a.m.Handcycles/Duos - 9:30 a.m.Professional Men - 9:37 a.m.Professional Women - 9:47 a.m.Para Athletics Division - 9:50 a.m.Wave 1 - 10:00 a.m.Wave 2 - 10:15 a.m.Wave 3 - 10:28 a.m.Wave 4 - 10:41 a.m.Wave 5 - 11:01 a.m.Wave 6 - 11:21 a.m.How many people run the Boston Marathon?More than 30,000 people from nearly 130 countries and all 50 states are expected to participate in the 130th Boston Marathon, according to organizers.This year, organizers elected to use six main starting waves rather than four as in past years.The overall field size of 30,000 participants is the same, but organizers said the new six-wave format will help optimize flow throughout the course.Each of the six waves will range in size from 3,200 to 7,100 athletes. The number of athletes per wave was determined based on a variety of factors, including estimated pace and finish time, the Boston Athletic Association said.They will have an army of supporters: the BAA estimates that more than 500,000 spectators will line the route.How to watch the 2026 Boston MarathonThe Boston Marathon will be broadcast nationwide on ESPN2 from 9 a.m. to 12:30 p.m. ET on April 20. ESPN will also carry some race coverage throughout the day.Those in the New England area can also watch live coverage beginning at 4 a.m. ET on their local ABC affiliate station, including: WCVB Channel 5, WMUR News 9 (Manchester, New Hampshire), WMTW Channel 8 (Portland, Maine) and WPTZ NBC5 (Burlington, Vermont/Plattsburgh, New York).Watch the Boston Marathon on ESPN2 with Fubo TV hereBoston Marathon course mapThe Boston Marathon start line is located in Hopkinton, which is west of the city.Runners traverse roads in towns and cities, including Ashland, Framingham, Natick, Wellesley, Newton and Brookline, before making their way to Boston.The finish line is located on Boylston Street in Boston.See the full course map on BAA's website.Melina Khan is a national trending reporter for USA TODAY. Keep up with her on X @melinakh and Instagram @bymelinakhan.",
